{"commands": [{"command": ["git", "-c", "core.preloadIndex=false", "--no-optional-locks", "show", ":udt_shared_readout_metric_constraint_campaign_2026-09-06/DECISION_BRIEF.md"], "returncode": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "# Decision brief \u2014 constraints gained without choosing physical content\n\nCampaign complete: five reviewed steps with caveats. All scientific results\nremain conditional candidates, UNPROMOTED; no sixth quota step was added.\n\nThe campaign examined all three proposed directions in five bounded steps:\none reviewed source/domain gate, three distinct mathematical investigations,\nand one targeted robustness follow-up. It did not continue the old completed\nG353--G356 campaign or add a sixth quota task.\n\n## What was learned\n\n| Direction | Additional constraint or distinction | What remains supplied/open |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shared ideal readouts, SC2 | One nonnegative label measure must explain overlapping queries jointly; separately positive readouts can be incompatible. In the declared finite constant-kernel class, feasibility is exactly y=A m with m>=0, equivalently its dual inequalities. | Geometry, common label registration, windows and rates are supplied; fine content remains free. No device identity follows. |\n| Joint metric responses, SC3 | A specified24-component timelike/null tide protocol obeys13 independent linear constraints and, if compatible, reconstructs one11-parameter algebraic Einstein curvature tensor. Timelike-only misses5 mixed components; null-only misses its scalar-curvature direction. | Actual smooth metric, frame and query normalization are supplied. Pointwise algebraic sufficiency is NOT complete Einstein Cauchy-data/PDE realization or an empirical readout law. |\n| Phase data/domain, SC4 | A noncritical real initial phase determines its full future-null initial covector and a unique local smooth phase. An everywhere-nonzero single real phase cannot cover an entire compact boundary-free spacelike slice. | Initial phase is ordinary data. Local duration/projection domain matters; global coverage is OPTIONAL. Product and curvature-recipe persistence are not derived. |\n| Robustness follow-up, SC5 | The overlap restriction survives bounded variable frequency weights, with an exact threshold for loss of uniform exclusion across that uncertainty class. | Bounds are conditional query/calibration data, not measured accuracy. Feasibility for some allowed weights is not feasibility for every fixed actual query. |\n\n### Precise framing for the simplest joint-content test\n\nFor exact transported windows P union Q, Q union R, P union R, common finite\nnonnegative mu, positive supplied reference rates r_i and normalized ideal\nrecords z_i=y_i/r_i, constant normalized weights1 give\n\n    z=(m_P+m_Q, m_Q+m_R, m_P+m_R).\n\nThus all three triangle inequalities are necessary and sufficient. The positive\nrecord (1,1,3) fails: m_Q=-1/2. Disjoint windows impose no such cross-record\nrestriction. Even compatible overlap records determine only the three cell\nmasses, not the entire measure.\n\nIf the active weights instead obey 1-e<=f_i(lambda)<=1+e with 0<=e<1,\nuniform necessity, and sufficiency over the declared uncertainty class, are\n\n    z_i>=0,  (1-e) z_i <= (1+e)(z_j+z_k).\n\nFor nonzero z>=0 the exact class threshold is\ne_*=max(0,2 max(z)/sum(z)-1); the zero record is separate.\n(1,1,3) remains excluded for every allowed kernel when e<1/5, but an exact\nallowed construction exists at1/5. Fixed unit weights still exclude it.\nThis is a mathematical20-percent boundary for the specified ideal-data\nuncertainty class, NOT an empirical calibration tolerance or instrument model.\n\n### Precise phase/data and metric boundaries\n\nFor a supplied smooth metric, spacelike slice with future unit normal n,\nspatial metric gamma and real initial phase phi, write a=n(Theta). Then\n\n    -a^2+|dphi|_gamma^2=0,   a=-|dphi|_gamma<0,\n    k|Sigma=dphi+|dphi|_gamma n-flat.\n\nThe local characteristic proof preserves the FULL ambient covector and its\naffinely geodesic raised gradient. It is valid only on a sufficiently small\nregular characteristic graph; a flat focusing control shows why cotangent\nflow existence alone does not supply a global single-valued phase.\nCompactness obstructs only the optional globally real nonzero coverage request,\nnot local G352 queries or admitted compact metric developments.\n\nSC3 is conditional on the bounded admitted Einstein arena Ric=Lambda g,\nnot on bare metric geometry alone. Its exact slot/sign convention, query\nscreens, thirteen equations and inverse are in step_03/CANDIDATE_ARGUMENT.md.\nIt uses tides g(R(X,k)k,Y), with Jacobi acceleration their negative, not\nG335's deformation q as a tidal acceleration. Arbitrary algebraic records\nare not declared realizable by G321's complete compact lawful data.\n\n## Assumptions and dependency ledger\n\n- Accepted scientific source pin:70034a6faa9264bf054eb473d5eb7a0889f3d2de.\n  G351/G352 remain OWNER_PROVISIONAL, with the continuous phase-independent\n  product CHOSEN. These support SC2/SC5; no physical measure is selected.\n- SC3 uses W4's working geometric interpretation, supplied Levi-Civita geometry,\n  G312's owner-provisional bounded response constitution and G348's generic\n  quotient/Jacobi definitions. The actual Einstein arena is load-bearing.\n- SC4's phase theorem uses smooth Lorentzian geometry and ordinary noncritical\n  initial phase data. Application to G321/G335 inherits their conditional\n  imported smooth-development theorem; no new metric solve or global theorem.\n- SC1 is a reviewed source map, not a theorem or new premise. It gates SC2/3/4;\n  reviewed SC2 then supports SC5. SC3 and SC4 are not dependencies of each other.\n- G353--G356 stay banked only at their previously reviewed conditional scope.\n  Their curvature recipes, optional naturality and fixed-label product\n  conditions do not become physically adopted or metric-selected laws.\n\n## Failed alternatives and remaining freedom\n\nSeparate readout positivity does not ensure common-content compatibility.\nSeparate null traces do not ensure one shared curvature tensor; both even\nshared-curvature and odd cyclic counterexamples survive those weaker checks.\nNull-only queries cannot recover the scalar channel in the Einstein arena.\nAn independently chosen normal phase derivative generally violates its type;\nsmooth metric/characteristic existence does not guarantee global real phase.\nUnconditional rejection of the diagnostic record fails once the weight\nuncertainty class reaches its threshold.\n\nOrdinary lawful initial metric data, local phase data, observers, labels,\nwindows, reference rates and compatible content distributions remain legitimate\nfree inputs. They need not be uniquely metric-selected. By contrast an actual\ndevice-output identity, a new counting rule or physical recipe adoption cannot\nbe hidden inside their definitions. No such new law was assumed.\n\nThe chosen curvature-current identity's persistence on a general admitted\nactual development remains OPEN; local free-phase propagation does not prove it.\nThe G352 physical-realization question remains: physical identification remains\nOPEN. No light, energy, particles, source population, matter, scale or canon\nwas selected. These are limits of the findings, not a proof that a new physical\npremise is necessary.\n\n## Verification and decision\n\nEach step received fresh separate-context source-first/direct adversarial review.\nExact model identity is UNKNOWN; different-model and human-specialist review\nare UNTESTED. Independent arguments/check implementations, same-code regression\nand finite examples are recorded separately. Analytic arguments own quantifiers.\nStep04's pre-freeze structural-symbolic equality failure was preserved and\ncorrected without formula/premise change. Step05 review exposed an actual\nreject-all-nonzero harness false pass; original evidence is retained and the\none permitted same-premise guard repair passed focused re-review. The reviewer\nindependently reapplied the original corruption and confirmed it now fails.\n\nFinal runtime checks: the full339-row premise audit passed (actual exit0,\n398.079937478s), and startup regression passed107 tests with its duplicate\nfull-audit test deselected. Four preservation hashes and all46 unrelated\nuntracked status entries match. Strict whole-diff whitespace checking retains\nan exit2 warning for four space-only lines in the immutable raw review diff;\nthe check excluding only that transcript passes. No raw evidence was altered.\nInitial final-fidelity review found only stale repair-status wording, corrected\nin the final log; its scientific-summary verdict and snapshots are retained.\nFinal factual-delta disposition is in CLOSURE_REVIEW_RECORD.md.\n\nRecommended next owner decision: consider conditional mathematical banking of\nthe reviewed SC2--SC5 families at exactly these scopes, with SC1 retained as a\nsource map. This campaign does not authorize or perform that promotion.\nNo physical commitment or new research campaign is requested by implication.\nBeyond this work order, no new campaign is authorized.\n\nThe three proposed directions have produced their distinguishing results and\nthe robustness follow-up answers a different limitation, so the campaign does\nnot spend its sixth slot on more examples. A further recipe-persistence or\nideal-to-observation interface investigation would need a new bounded target;\nthe present findings do not require choosing photons, energy or a familiar\nmechanism. The next substantive scientific choice belongs to Charles.\n\nPreservation: fixed through-G352 manuscript/coverage sidecar,339-row registry\nand CANON hashes remain unchanged. Backup completeness and pre-reboot unsaved-\nstate disposition remain UNVERIFIED. ScratchDisk blocks archive-dependent tasks\nonly and was not used. Protected payloads were not inspected; all46 unrelated\nuntracked status entries remain visible. No disk/infrastructure work occurred.\n"}, {"command": ["git", "-c", "core.preloadIndex=false", "--no-optional-locks", "show", ":udt_shared_readout_metric_constraint_campaign_2026-09-06/CAMPAIGN_LOG.md"], "returncode": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "# Adaptive campaign \u2014 compact log\n\nStatus: COMPLETE at the five-reviewed-step scientific scope; final preservation\nhandoff follows this record. All five steps reviewed with caveats; no result promoted.\nBudget: six substantive reviewed steps or eight hours; start22:02:38 UTC\n2026-09-06, deadline06:02:38 UTC2026-09-07.\n\n## Startup\n\n- Actual HEAD70034a6f, grok synchronized by fetch/ff-only pull; tracked clean.\n- All46 unrelated untracked status entries preserved; payloads not inspected.\n- Required current startup chain and triggered scope/provenance/verification\n  protocols read; orientation reported before package creation or research.\n- Full339-row premise audit completed with actual exit0 under2 GiB/900s.\n  Tool capture is in STARTUP_CHECK_RECORD.json; no elapsed duration or\n  separated stdout/stderr stream is invented for this initial invocation.\n- Prior campaign complete and G353--G356 conditionally banked, not physical\n  identification. Manuscript remains its fixed through-G352 edition.\n- Baseline self-contained startup regression:107 passed,1 long-audit test\n  deselected because the actual full audit was already run separately. Exact\n  command, stdout/stderr,1.606655709s subprocess timing and512MiB/60s limits\n  are in startup_regression.*. No old test or guard was changed.\n- A first compact registry query used incorrect column names and displayed\n  redundant wide selected rows; corrected to ID/term/controlling-source columns.\n  No registry content changed and no scientific conclusion used the bad display.\n\n## Step allocation\n\n1. REVIEWED-WITH-CAVEATS: source-domain/measurement-interface screen, SC1-READOUT,\n   SC1-METRIC, SC1-PHASE-DOMAIN. Source16/freeze2 hash checks passed.\n   Argument SHA2566fd638a600a6ef59125001471d432c463201179713811f6b74a25642e1850583.\n   Fresh reviewer tri_step01_review completed source-first then direct\n   adversarial review: no required defect,0/1 repairs. Main read both reports\n   before downstream work. No reviewer conclusions received before author freeze.\n   Candidate/work order checkpoint06d523db committed and pushed; HEAD/origin\n   divergence0/0. Subsequent git-source authentication matched all16 sources\n   to70034a6f. Source hashes are correspondence evidence, not scientific proof.\n2. REVIEWED-WITH-CAVEATS: SC2-CONE, SC2-OVERLAP, SC2-INVISIBLE; fresh\n   tri_step02_review found no required defect,0/1 repairs. Argument SHA256\n   41bb97aa12ba9d8e30d34d73a324095103a54c520d154889a8b514c1f036b5cf.\n   Author22 exact guard groups passed; all4 changed-formula paths failed\n   intended guards. No unexpected failure. No reviewer findings before freeze.\n   Main read both full reports and verified the37-file/36-payload archive.\n   Retained caveat: author's disjoint-control arithmetic identity is regression,\n   not independent feasibility proof; analytic/independent evidence survives.\n3. REVIEWED-WITH-CAVEATS: SC3-COMPATIBILITY/RECONSTRUCTION/BLINDNESS, fresh\n   tri_step03_review found no required defect,0/1 repairs. Argument SHA256\n   1d9ec37b3c7cbec4c308ea2177a824077052a2b5541cb34e23e005730a21d903.\n   Author15 exact groups passed, ranks11/13/6/10;4 real formula mutants failed\n   expected guards. No unexpected author failure or reviewer finding before freeze.\n   Main read complete reports, verified35-file/34-payload archive; independent\n   generic bivector construction confirms image/annihilator and blind directions.\n   Retain hard-coded normalization and orbit-symmetry regression limitations.\n   Uses reviewed SC1 and accepted sources, NOT SC2.\n4. REVIEWED-WITH-CAVEATS: initial phase compatibility/local propagation/compact-domain gate,\n   per step_04/QUESTION.md. Uses reviewed SC1 and accepted sources, NOT SC2/SC3.\n   Independent construction while SC3 review runs is not downstream use of\n   an unreviewed scientific result. Argument SHA256\n   42f4c5881c9bf2f914b7682e50b030a30e50784fc9a671b2c77a2f427ff944ad.\n   First author check failed at structural symbolic matrix equality; frozen\n   solver-first diagnostic proved all entry differences zero. Preserved original\n   code/failure; exact entrywise comparison correction changed no formula or\n   premise. Rerun18 groups passed;4 actual mutants failed expected guards.\n   Fresh tri_step04_review passed with no required scientific defect,0/1 review\n   repairs. Main read complete reports and authenticated47 files/46 payloads.\n   Source-first independent18 controls, full proof scrutiny and exact initial/\n   corrected/mutant replays passed; critical-normal guard limitation retained.\n5. REVIEWED-WITH-CAVEATS: robustness of shared overlap constraints to bounded supplied\n   frequency-weight uncertainty; step_05/QUESTION.md. Uses reviewed SC2 only,\n   not pending SC4. This tests a limitation of SC2, not a quota example.\n   Argument SHA25650c7f90558bc623f227d5066a84a876017c563218f38426fd7e2f7a80fa5c7c9.\n   Author16 exact groups/1262 assertions passed;625 signed record controls,\n   182 constructed and443 rejected. Four actual formula mutants failed expected\n   guards. No unexpected author failure. tri_step05_review sealed its source-first\n   argument/checks before direct review; no findings were received before freeze.\n   Reviewer reported a real author harness false pass: rejecting every nonzero\n   record could pass. Initial analytic argument survives; one same-premise\n   verification repair was required and completed. Initial frozen code/evidence stays intact;\n   repaired script adds explicit returned-status feasibility guard and real\n   reject_nonzero mutant. Baseline17 groups/1887 assertions passes; new mutant\n   fails expected guard. Focused re-review passed; original corruption independently\n   reapplied and caught. Main read all reports and authenticated initial40/39 and\n   focused38/37 archive-file/payload counts.1/1 repair allowance used.\n6. Unallocated; no useful distinct remaining step presumed.\n\n## Preservation boundary\n\nBackup completeness and pre-reboot unsaved-state disposition UNVERIFIED.\nScratchDisk not used; protected work, premises, canon and manuscript excluded.\n\n## Checkpoint / return plan\n\nCheckpoint a4655f39 preserves reviewed SC2/SC3 and frozen SC4 plus its initial\nimplementation failure; committed/pushed, observed HEAD/origin divergence0/0.\nSC4/SC5 frozen/source hash checks and accepted-source Git comparisons passed.\nNo final result is inferred from those correspondence checks.\nAll scientific reviews are complete as of23:08:34 UTC,65m56s from campaign start.\nStep06 is deliberately unallocated: all three directions yielded distinguishing\nresults and the one robustness follow-up addresses their concrete query limit.\nNo further quota example or open-ended recipe/measurement investigation begun.\nFinal work is evidence/fidelity\nreview, operational-pointer refresh, preservation/startup checks and candidate\ncommit/push; not scientific banking. Stop for a load-bearing unresolved objection.\n\n## Closure evidence and return\n\n- Scientific/review artifacts through the completed SC4/SC5 reviews and check\n  repair were committed/pushed at e93f49ebc92d527a39f04c4ce72c51408f74b679;\n  observed HEAD/origin divergence0/0. The final containing commit adds reviewed\n  operational pointers, this brief/log and closure evidence, not new science.\n- Full final339-row premise audit PASS, actual exit0,398.079937478s,\n  105792KiB maximum child RSS,2GiB/900s caps, empty stderr, no timeout.\n  Separate stdout/stderr and exact argv/wrapper/version are retained in\n  closure_premise_audit.*. Its repository archive-integrity checks do not\n  verify external backups or ScratchDisk.\n- Final self-contained startup regression:107 passed,1 deselected in1.64s;\n  actual subprocess1.726905716s. Only the duplicate full-audit test was omitted\n  because that audit ran separately. No test/instruction/scientific source changed.\n- All four preservation hashes match; all46 unrelated untracked status entries\n  match the startup metadata. Tracked changes stay within this package plus\n  LIVE/HANDOFF/CURRENT_RESEARCH_PROGRAM/INDEX/MEMORY operational updates.\n- Initial final-fidelity review passed scientific/root-summary scope with one\n  packaging finding P1: stale repair-underway wording. Corrected to completed\n  history here; candidate/reviewer originals unchanged. The initial17-file\n  archive and16 payload hashes match; its report preserves snapshots of the\n  initial brief/log/roots. CLOSURE_REVIEW_INPUT_SHA256SUMS is historical after\n  this factual delta, not a current-file pass claim.\n- Strict whole-diff whitespace check remains exit2 for four space-only context\n  lines in the preserved raw unified-diff review transcript. Excluding ONLY\n  that immutable transcript gives exit0. WHITESPACE_CHECK_DISPOSITION.json\n  retains both actual results; raw evidence was not sanitized.\n- The manuscript's known stock live339/fixed335 input mismatch is not repaired,\n  rerun or relabeled as passed. This campaign checks its unchanged bytes, not\n  a fresh full fixed-edition review.\n\nScientific steps finished23:08:34 UTC (65m56s); final runtime/preservation checks\nfinished by23:19:40 UTC (77m02s). No resource/access or unresolved scientific-review\nblocker remains. Final factual-delta fidelity and containing commit/push are\nrecorded in CLOSURE_REVIEW_RECORD.md and the final handoff, without reopening science.\nNext owner decision: conditional mathematical promotion of SC2--SC5 at exact\nreviewed scope, not physical recipe adoption; SC1 remains a source map.\nNo sixth step, new physical law, scientific banking or further campaign begun.\n"}, {"command": ["git", "-c", "core.preloadIndex=f